{
  "what": "The world list a series' zone is chosen from: how each listed zone is named, how a search folds and matches, the offsets and the order of the list, and where a stored or a device zone stands in it — the answers cal_core::zone_list must give.",
  "why": "The list, its names and its search are rules, and each surface would otherwise write its own: a city split one way on the desktop and another on the phone, an umlaut folded here and not there, Dublin sorted beside London on one device and beside Paris on the other. One list in the core answers both, and a frontend that is not JavaScript.",
  "decidedBy": "DESIGN-series-time-zone.md, section \"Die Zonenliste\", and Toni's decisions 17b (the full list, generated from chrono-tz), 25b (merged places found by search as \"Berlin (auch Oslo)\"), 26a (one rule for zones), 29a (order by standard time as of today: the smallest offset in the year from today), 30a (a fixed order: standard offset, then city), 31a (\"+5\" means UTC+05:00 only) and 32a (built on tzdata 2025b).",
  "writtenBy": [
    "By hand, from the tzdata chrono-tz 0.10.4 ships (release 2025b): the zone files for offsets, `backward` and `etcetera` for the links and their kinds. Chosen, not measured: the rules are new. Newer tzdata releases disagree with 2025b for Casablanca and El_Aaiun from 2026-09-20, for Vancouver, Edmonton and Inuvik from 2026-11-01, and for Chisinau's transition times. No `at` instant falls on those dates. A standard offset reads the year after `today`, which does cross them, so no row pins the standard offset or the place in the order of those zones unless both releases agree (Casablanca's 0). A tzdata update then turns no row red for a reason that is not the code's."
  ],
  "readBy": [
    "crates/cal-core/src/zone_list.rs (every row; the offsets, the order and the search rows with offsets only with the `zones` feature)",
    "crates/cal-ffi/src/lib.rs (labels, notListed, search with offsets, choice, offsets and order, through the phone's doors; the fold rows are the core's alone, since no door hands out the fold)",
    "src/intl/zoneList.contract.test.ts (labels, notListed, the search rows without offsets and choice, through the WebAssembly door and the shared shell; the offsets come from the host there)"
  ],
  "whereItLives": {
    "note": "Inside cal-core, like seriesClock.json: twelve adapter repositories compile cal-core, and an include_str! reaching out of the crate would break the day it moves. A crate reads its own files."
  },
  "notInThisTable": "Whether a device's clock library can use a zone (the shell's Intl check), the words each surface writes (the offset's form \"UTC−04:00\", region names, the count line), and which rows open the list (\"Aktuell\", \"Dieses Gerät\"): later stages of the design.",
  "shape": {
    "regions": "the region names a search question carries, in German and English, as the translations name them",
    "labels": "[{zone, city, area, region}]: listed zones and their parts",
    "notListed": "names that must not be entries of the list",
    "fold": "[{text, folded}]: the search's folding, pinned on its own",
    "search": "[{query, regions, offsets?, hits? | count? | includes?, excludes?, note}]: `offsets` is {at, today} when the row needs the list's offsets (then only with the `zones` feature); `hits` is every hit, in list order; `count` the number of hits; `includes` hits that must be among them (order not pinned), `excludes` zones that must not be. A hit is {zone, via, also?}: zone is the tzdata id or \"utc\" for the UTC entry; via one match field per word; also {label, name?, kind?} the other name a word found it by.",
    "offsets": "[{zone, at, today, seconds, sign?, hh?, mm?, standard?, note?}]: a listed zone's offset at `at` (sign, hh and mm in whole minutes, as the list writes it) and, when given, its standard offset as of `today` (seconds)",
    "order": "[{at, today, head, tail, utcBefore}]: the first and last zones of the list, and the zone the UTC entry opens",
    "choice": "[{stored?, device?, expect}]: expect is {stored, device?} with each {kind: utc | listed | not_listed | unreadable, zone?, name?, canonical?}"
  },
